feat(v1.1): one-command local launchers and the user guide

Windows (start-local.bat) and macOS/Linux (start-local.sh) launchers that:
- bind 127.0.0.1 only; never 0.0.0.0;
- enable local uploads for that process, keep AI and public mode off;
- check Python 3.12+ and the project dependencies via scripts/check_env.py;
- ask before running pip install, and change no system environment variables;
- print the local URL and how to stop.

The environment check lives in Python so the batch file never has to embed < or >
(cmd treats them as redirection, which is what broke the first draft).

Also adds docs/release-1.1/USER_GUIDE.md (download, start, upload, read a finding,
accept/reject, export, stop, limits, privacy, troubleshooting) and links it from the
README.

Removes the stray .commitmsg that was accidentally committed in 4aa0b32; it contained
only the commit text, no secrets, but it does not belong in the release tree.

tests/test_launchers.py pins the contract: loopback bind, uploads on, AI off, public
off, prompt before install, no secrets printed, LF shell script, bash -n where bash
exists.

484 passed, 2 skipped; Ruff clean.
